// Title: Potential Arbitrary DLL Load Using Winword
// Sigma ID: f7375e28-5c14-432f-b8d1-1db26c832df3
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Victor Sergeev, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-09 | Modified: 2023-03-29
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1202
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading using the Microsoft Office winword process via the '/l' flag.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/D4Vinci/One-Lin3r/blob/9fdfa5f0b9c698dfbd4cdfe7d2473192777ae1c6/one_lin3r/core/liners/windows/cmd/dll_loader_word.py
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_office_winword_dll_load.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\WINWORD.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "WinWord.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/l " and ProcessCommandLine contains ".dll")
